{
  "comment": [
    "Every way this deployment can reach a language model, one record per proxy.",
    "A proxy is who we call and which credential we present \u2014 not who provided the model.",
    "Claude is provided by Anthropic whether we buy it direct or through Vercel's gateway.",
    "Adding a proxy is a record here plus its credential in the environment. No code change:",
    "every field below either names data (a URL, an env name, a model name) or selects one of a",
    "finite set of named operations that already exist in code. The operation vocabularies are",
    "listed in model_configuration_schema.ts, and tsc checks this file on every build.",
    "Model names are read from `<prefix>_MODEL` for agent runs and `<prefix>_<USE_CASE>_MODEL`",
    "for every other use case, with the prefix each proxy declares below.",
    "Several proxies reach the same model, so `offer_models_made_by` names the single proxy the",
    "catalog lists each model provider through: we buy Anthropic and OpenAI direct, and reach",
    "every other model provider through the gateway. A model provider whose direct proxy has no",
    "credential configured falls to the first configured proxy flagged",
    "`offer_models_no_other_proxy_offers`, in the order of this file."
  ],
  "model_catalog_sources": {
    "models_dev": {
      "fetch_from": "https://models.dev/api.json",
      "refresh_after_ms": 86400000,
      "retry_after_failure_ms": 300000,
      "request_timeout_ms": 10000
    }
  },
